# Belt and braces. The root .gitignore already covers these, but this file
# lives next to the thing that holds a real credential, so it is repeated here
# deliberately — a second rule costs nothing and a leaked key costs a rotation.
# It also travels with the folder when the spike moves to the take-home repo,
# which will be public.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated by the spikes. spike.py records the account balance in its auth
# step, so any findings file can carry it — glob rather than name them, because
# the next spike will invent another filename.
findings*.json
